<title>JAPAN: Isuzu bid-only on news of GM diesel talks.</title>
<headline>Isuzu bid-only on news of GM diesel talks.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Isuzu Motors Ltd shares were bid-only in early Thursday morning trade on news that Isuzu and General Motors Corp of the United States were considering transferring GM's diesel engine development and production to Isuzu, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0030 GMT, the shares were bid-only at 397 yen, compared with 387 yen at the end of trade on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Isuzu also said the two companies had agreed that Isuzu will produce 1,700cc diesel engines at its Poland factory for GM affiliate Adam Opel AG starting in 2000.</p>
</text>
